00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:37.650
April, 1590 - Sagami Province - Kamakura - Kōtoku Temple

00:01:38.690 --> 00:01:39.380
Milord!

00:01:41.450 --> 00:01:44.980
Just now Hōjō's forces in Tamanawa Castle have surrendered.

00:01:46.070 --> 00:01:49.700
It hasn't even been two days since we left Odawara!

00:01:50.150 --> 00:01:56.040
There is a man from Mino called Hanshichi who has some tea tools to show you.

00:01:56.580 --> 00:01:58.840
Then we must hurry!

00:01:59.190 --> 00:01:59.770
Yes.

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:11.760
Seems like my expedition is extending to Musashi.

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:15.340
Please keep me safe.

00:02:21.230 --> 00:02:22.640
Dear Buddha.

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:27.020
Edo Frontier

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:33.200
Why are Toyotomi's troops always so slow?

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:37.880
If we are intent on attacking Musashi,

00:02:38.150 --> 00:02:41.380
we need both Tokugawa and Toyotomi's troops to work together.

00:02:42.210 --> 00:02:47.460
If we don't succeed, then I, Honda Tadakatsu, will not be able to face my master Lord Tokugawa.

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:51.880
I think we should pass on this.

00:02:52.170 --> 00:02:58.660
If Toyotomi takes all the credit, then I wouldn't know what to say to Lord Tokugawa.

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:03.510
Let me see what you're made of then, Lord Oribe.

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:10.640
You want me to spread the word that you are a piece of shit daimyo?

00:03:17.090 --> 00:03:19.280
We'll head east tomorrow.

00:03:19.510 --> 00:03:23.450
Take care of those small castles that stand in our way.

00:03:27.570 --> 00:03:31.220
Hmm... Me and my big mouth.

00:03:32.390 --> 00:03:36.990
Why are Tokugawa's men so short-tempered?

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:44.770
These are marvelous drawings.

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:49.540
Master Hasegawa Tōhaku spent a lot of energy on them.

00:03:54.820 --> 00:03:57.850
Use these as examples and let some kids help you out.

00:04:00.230 --> 00:04:03.510
Find some shitty brats to draw them.

00:04:03.860 --> 00:04:06.800
These are too perfect. The painter will get attached to them.

00:04:06.860 --> 00:04:08.910
I sense no imperfection from them.

00:04:09.460 --> 00:04:13.420
Keep that in mind when we plan to sell some at the market.

00:04:14.760 --> 00:04:19.430
I understand. I'll return to Mino and make some new ones.

00:04:19.490 --> 00:04:23.730
Wait. Leave one with me.

00:04:23.910 --> 00:04:26.390
Oh... Okay.

00:04:37.480 --> 00:04:41.220
The Next Day - Musashi Province - Setagaya Castle

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:51.030
Will he be okay? Lord Oribe went inside to negotiate.

00:04:51.230 --> 00:04:52.400
I wonder about that.

00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:58.260
This place has been controlled by the Kira family for centuries.

00:04:58.340 --> 00:05:00.360
They won't go down easily.

00:05:00.920 --> 00:05:06.370
It's good to have him taste pain once in a while. Let us continue east.

00:05:23.740 --> 00:05:27.460
We will definitely treat you well after you surrender.

00:05:27.830 --> 00:05:32.360
You just have to give up the castle.

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:38.600
This tea bowl will be yours, under the Kira name.

00:05:42.590 --> 00:05:47.820
I can hear it. The sound of your swallowing.

00:05:48.870 --> 00:05:51.560
The bowl is above your head.

00:05:53.790 --> 00:05:57.330
Let me hear you scream.

00:06:05.730 --> 00:06:07.310
Let me take a look.

00:06:08.930 --> 00:06:10.240
What are those stirrups?

00:06:10.940 --> 00:06:15.270
Our ancestors received them when we signed an agreement with Ōta Dōkan.

00:06:15.270 --> 00:06:18.270
They're the family treasure, the Musashi Stirrups.

00:06:19.540 --> 00:06:21.110
Anything wrong with them?

00:06:21.530 --> 00:06:22.530
Nothing.

00:06:24.770 --> 00:06:30.100
Wow...Such an simple elegance, with an unbridled rich color.

00:06:30.390 --> 00:06:32.850
The eastern lands possessed such imperfect objects.

00:06:36.100 --> 00:06:38.820
I was looking for some Musashi souvenirs.

00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:42.690
Those would be perfect to cheer Master up!

00:06:46.120 --> 00:06:49.940
If I give up Setagaya Castle, will you really give this to me?

00:06:50.020 --> 00:06:53.920
No, just surrendering the castle won't be enough.

00:06:55.330 --> 00:06:58.000
If you don't give up those stirrups to the Chief Advisor,

00:06:58.060 --> 00:07:00.710
we will attack you with full force.

00:07:12.190 --> 00:07:15.070
You bastard! That's not what you said before!

00:07:15.460 --> 00:07:19.310
How about? You in or not?

00:07:20.890 --> 00:07:25.420
Those stirrups represent the soul of a Kanto warrior! They're our pride!

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:30.290
To give them up is to give up my dignity as a warrior!

00:07:32.160 --> 00:07:33.920
Who gives a shit about this shitty bowl!

00:07:35.130 --> 00:07:39.820
Just sell it at some crappy stall!

00:07:53.700 --> 00:07:56.790
How... How did this happen...

00:07:58.060 --> 00:08:00.390
You dastardly plebian samurai!

00:08:01.110 --> 00:08:02.890
Plebian samurai!?

00:08:03.200 --> 00:08:05.770
Did you just call me a plebian samurai!?

00:08:06.120 --> 00:08:07.430
Unforgivable!

00:08:07.760 --> 00:08:09.570
Men! Get over here!

00:08:22.670 --> 00:08:24.720
I'll fight to the death, then!

00:08:24.940 --> 00:08:27.810
All the way to the bitter end!

00:08:30.880 --> 00:08:34.660
If you kill me, then that will be the end of the Kira clan.

00:08:35.340 --> 00:08:38.750
You know who's right outside your castle walls.

00:08:39.920 --> 00:08:42.860
The elite warrior of Toyotomi, Asano Danjyō!

00:08:45.370 --> 00:08:49.390
And also Tokugawa's most ruthless commander, Honda Tadakatsu!

00:08:50.140 --> 00:08:55.390
Honda's on very good terms with me, like husband and wife!

00:08:55.510 --> 00:08:56.490
You idiot.

00:08:57.810 --> 00:09:03.450
If anything should happen to me, count your clan as good as dead.

00:09:04.280 --> 00:09:07.010
What kind of warrior wants that to happen!?

00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:10.290
Ōta Dōkan must be rolling in his grave!

00:09:14.930 --> 00:09:16.250
I won't repeat myself again.

00:09:16.460 --> 00:09:18.080
Hand over the stirrups.

00:09:18.820 --> 00:09:22.240
That is the only way I can guarantee your safety.

00:09:30.210 --> 00:09:31.240
Hurry up!

00:09:45.140 --> 00:09:48.920
Lord Oribe has captured Kira and is bringing him here!

00:09:49.180 --> 00:09:49.980
What!?

00:10:08.390 --> 00:10:10.020
Sorry about that.

00:10:10.120 --> 00:10:15.270
I'm a "piece of shit daimyo" so I pass a lot of gas.

00:10:32.960 --> 00:10:35.910
I wonder if the other army is doing well.

00:10:36.610 --> 00:10:41.080
I told Tadakatsu and the others that Musashi will become our new paradise.

00:10:41.620 --> 00:10:44.150
He'll be sure to work hard.

00:10:45.220 --> 00:10:46.610
Milord! Look!

00:10:50.190 --> 00:10:52.380
I wanted to take a look before heading inside the castle.

00:10:53.120 --> 00:10:57.820
We'll be working with them in the future, the people of Edo.

00:11:01.040 --> 00:11:04.620
Beginning of May, 1590 - Sagami Province - Kamakura - Tsurugaoka Hachiman Temple

00:11:12.970 --> 00:11:17.920
Only you and I were able to conquer the nation, even with our meager backgrounds.

00:11:18.520 --> 00:11:22.790
But you descended from Genji himself.

00:11:23.130 --> 00:11:26.290
You had a lot of help.

00:11:28.260 --> 00:11:29.660
That's why...

00:11:34.330 --> 00:11:37.930
I win, Minamoto no Yoritomo!

00:11:38.640 --> 00:11:44.010
If I may interject, there is a dangerous man underneath you trying to rebel.

00:11:47.320 --> 00:11:52.890
He is the very man people place worth on, Sen no Rikyū.

00:11:57.070 --> 00:11:58.380
I know that.

00:11:59.180 --> 00:12:00.520
Listen, Mitsunari.

00:12:00.580 --> 00:12:05.150
You dealt with Sōji better than Hidenaga or Rikyū.

00:12:05.870 --> 00:12:07.880
Work hard when you attack Jōshū!

00:12:08.260 --> 00:12:13.190
Show everyone what you've got, or else you'll never sway those who still admire Rikyū!

00:12:13.620 --> 00:12:17.130
I, Mitsunari, will perform my duties without fail.

00:12:18.620 --> 00:12:20.370
Our sightseeing here at Kamakura is over!

00:12:25.120 --> 00:12:26.890
How does it look, Lord Ieyasu?

00:12:27.620 --> 00:12:32.480
I will chop down all of the surrounding trees when the main tower is finished.

00:12:32.610 --> 00:12:36.730
Odawara Castle will then be able to see this castle loud and clear.

00:12:36.930 --> 00:12:41.760
Hōjō will be scared shitless at how we built this castle in one night.

00:12:42.480 --> 00:12:45.090
I am awed by your tenacity.

00:12:45.450 --> 00:12:49.040
Let me give you an update on our forces.

00:12:49.720 --> 00:12:52.860
Odawara Castle has been completely surrounded.

00:12:53.210 --> 00:12:58.150
Hōjō's long reign over Kanto is coming to an end.

00:12:59.470 --> 00:13:03.100
Only Oū remains. And then...

00:13:08.530 --> 00:13:09.740
Come with me.

00:13:14.140 --> 00:13:16.010
How does this look?

00:13:17.280 --> 00:13:21.810
Pummeling Odawara Castle with my "water cannon" feels pretty good.

00:13:23.490 --> 00:13:24.860
Excuse me.

00:13:30.550 --> 00:13:32.950
Say, Lord Ieyasu.

00:13:33.370 --> 00:13:37.030
You're actually aiming for the heavens, aren't you?

00:13:40.170 --> 00:13:46.470
I wouldn't have given up my lands and came all the way here to Kanto.

00:13:47.130 --> 00:13:51.200
If we must fight, then we must protect Tōkai, which is closer to Kyoto.

00:13:51.570 --> 00:13:54.490
That is what I really think.

00:13:54.760 --> 00:13:56.480
Please consider my opinion.

00:14:04.030 --> 00:14:09.290
I see how strong your "water cannon" is. You are not lying to me.

00:14:09.930 --> 00:14:12.680
Please take care of Japan, then.

00:14:14.220 --> 00:14:19.900
I want to follow Lord Nobunaga's ambitions and expand towards Korea and China.

00:14:20.360 --> 00:14:24.010
I wanted to leave Kyoto with my eldest, Tsurumatsu.

00:14:24.170 --> 00:14:25.810
But he's much too young.

00:14:26.340 --> 00:14:31.990
If you can look after him, then I can go off in peace.

00:14:32.830 --> 00:14:39.230
I willl one day lead all of Japan, Korea, and China.

00:14:47.390 --> 00:14:51.310
My days are numbered. I am over fifty already.

00:14:53.940 --> 00:14:56.010
I'm asking you, Lord Ieyasu.

00:14:57.880 --> 00:15:01.790
Do not betray me like Akechi.

00:15:04.770 --> 00:15:06.810
That was close yesterday.

00:15:07.620 --> 00:15:10.320
If your "water cannon" had wavered a little bit,

00:15:10.470 --> 00:15:14.180
our disagreement with Toyotomi would have been revealed.

00:15:14.590 --> 00:15:16.360
I did not lie.

00:15:16.690 --> 00:15:19.230
Please keep this in your minds.

00:15:20.370 --> 00:15:23.840
I do not wish to control the heavens through force.

00:15:29.610 --> 00:15:32.430
Milord, your guest is here.

00:15:35.990 --> 00:15:38.490
Thank you for coming all the way out here from Kawagoe.

00:15:38.570 --> 00:15:42.620
Zuifū, no, Tenkai the Monk.

00:15:44.760 --> 00:15:46.720
It has been a long time.

00:16:16.910 --> 00:16:23.750
I was able to turn from a mere disciple at Mt. Hiei to a head monk at Kawagoe Temple.

00:16:24.080 --> 00:16:28.960
I am eternally indebted to you, Lord Ieyasu.

00:16:32.100 --> 00:16:33.940
We can talk about the past later.

00:16:34.590 --> 00:16:36.550
Let us see what you've painted.

00:16:41.360 --> 00:16:47.220
I used the ancient Tang dynasty capital as a blueprint to paint the future Edo Castle.

00:16:47.870 --> 00:16:50.530
A blue dragon lines the east, towards Hirakawa.

00:16:51.660 --> 00:16:54.440
A white tiger lines the west, towards Tōkaidō.

00:16:55.730 --> 00:16:59.430
A phoenix lines the south, towards Hibiya.

00:17:00.240 --> 00:17:02.490
A black tortoise lines the north, towards Mt. Fuji.

00:17:03.680 --> 00:17:07.780
This is the best location to set up the capital of Kanto.

00:17:23.470 --> 00:17:26.510
As of now, Odawara's ships have difficulties in reaching Kamakura.

00:17:27.080 --> 00:17:29.240
This place is strategically fortified.

00:17:29.550 --> 00:17:33.830
And it can become an important place for trade.

00:17:34.550 --> 00:17:38.630
Moving the capital to Kanto is akin to our death!

00:17:39.190 --> 00:17:43.540
You dare go against that in order to build a capital of such grandeur?

00:17:43.940 --> 00:17:46.040
I am completely floored!

00:17:46.510 --> 00:17:50.890
The late Akechi allowed us to have such ambitions.

00:17:51.310 --> 00:17:52.790
Isn't that right, Master Tenkai?

00:18:00.490 --> 00:18:03.160
Let us make Edo the paradise we yearn for!

00:18:03.870 --> 00:18:12.020
It will be the culmination of military, agriculture, business, and aesthetics,

00:18:12.190 --> 00:18:15.120
leading us to a thousand years of peace.

00:18:17.500 --> 00:18:20.550
Edo will become the true capital of justice.

00:18:20.770 --> 00:18:23.140
The world will gravitate towards us.

00:18:35.860 --> 00:18:39.430
Musashi Province - Toshima District

00:18:43.870 --> 00:18:47.010
How should I write this letter to the Master?

00:18:48.030 --> 00:18:51.090
I've already decided to give him these Musashi Stirrups.

00:18:53.800 --> 00:18:57.940
In the Tales of Ise, what comes after "Musashi Stirrups" is the word "As expected..."

00:18:59.750 --> 00:19:03.840
"As expected... As expected of..."

00:19:14.600 --> 00:19:17.180
Edo is such a wilderness.

00:19:19.190 --> 00:19:24.400
I'm not like the deceased Lord Takigawa, though I still don't wish to live here.

00:19:25.930 --> 00:19:30.660
The Toshima District shall now be under the rule of Toyotomi.

00:19:31.070 --> 00:19:34.580
I bring the letter of law from the Chief Advisor himself.

00:19:35.370 --> 00:19:40.470
Any uprisings will be dealt with immediately.

00:19:44.620 --> 00:19:46.980
You're Tarō, right?

00:19:48.240 --> 00:19:51.470
Any beautiful scenery around here?

00:19:51.560 --> 00:19:53.040
Nope, nope.

00:19:53.310 --> 00:19:56.930
I guess there are those seven pine trees over there.

00:20:04.770 --> 00:20:07.030
I should find something else to talk about in my letter.

00:20:08.900 --> 00:20:11.080
Is there a name for this land?

00:20:11.520 --> 00:20:12.980
Nope, nope.

00:20:13.930 --> 00:20:16.450
I'll make up a name, then.

00:20:18.860 --> 00:20:20.340
Let's see...

00:20:20.610 --> 00:20:23.510
If an aesthete would name this wilderness...

00:20:28.130 --> 00:20:30.890
Let's call this place Nanahongi!

00:20:31.260 --> 00:20:35.010
It is an excellent name, fit for an aesthete.

00:20:39.160 --> 00:20:42.000
How are we gonna build that sign for the laws?

00:20:42.410 --> 00:20:46.180
The previous lord took away all of our lumbar.

00:20:46.430 --> 00:20:49.880
Cut those pine trees down, then.

00:20:51.110 --> 00:20:54.040
Even names can be elegant.

00:20:55.210 --> 00:21:01.670
Nanahongi shall be famous one day!

00:21:12.470 --> 00:21:17.120
(I have no idea if this really happened, from 7 to 6, Nana to Roppongi.)

00:21:18.390 --> 00:21:22.000
Sagami Province - Sōun Temple Mountain

00:21:25.040 --> 00:21:28.700
We've received a top-quality bamboo, Master.

00:21:30.890 --> 00:21:32.850
What did Lord Oribe write?

00:21:43.790 --> 00:21:45.380
He finally smiled.

00:21:51.850 --> 00:21:53.100
Here, have some medicine.

00:21:56.700 --> 00:22:00.740
The house of simplicity at Enomura is finished.

00:22:01.010 --> 00:22:04.820
It is a marvelous piece of work, like you wanted.

00:22:06.380 --> 00:22:08.660
The Chief Advisor is cruel, though.

00:22:09.390 --> 00:22:13.640
He wants you who's sick in bed to take part in the tea ceremony.

00:22:16.690 --> 00:22:18.810
I'll take my leave, then.

00:22:31.790 --> 00:22:36.290
These flies are so annoying.

00:22:37.020 --> 00:22:38.680
I don't see any flies, though.

00:23:03.780 --> 00:23:06.510
Everytime I　

00:23:03.780 --> 00:23:06.510
Anata no mune

00:23:06.670 --> 00:23:08.900
feel your heart

00:23:06.670 --> 00:23:08.900
Fureru sonotabi

00:23:09.630 --> 00:23:14.990
Your burning, sincere passion singes me.

00:23:09.630 --> 00:23:14.990
Yakedoshisou na shinshi na jounetsu

00:23:15.910 --> 00:23:21.170
Were the world to turn against you, my dear love

00:23:15.910 --> 00:23:21.170
Sekai juu wo teki ni mawashitatte

00:23:22.020 --> 00:23:27.330
Oppose its rotation and return to me.

00:23:22.020 --> 00:23:27.330
Mezashitanara douzo tsuranuite kudasai

00:23:28.170 --> 00:23:33.420
Men are alike butterflies, as women are alike flowers.

00:23:28.170 --> 00:23:33.420
Otoko wa chouchou de onna wa hana de

00:23:34.420 --> 00:23:37.300
Through heaven and earth,

00:23:34.420 --> 00:23:37.300
Kuu to daichi to demo

00:23:37.530 --> 00:23:40.880
Are also alike, we all choose to live.

00:23:37.530 --> 00:23:40.880
Onaji asu wo eraberuno

00:23:41.080 --> 00:23:46.750
Should we be seperated by the flow of time?

00:23:41.080 --> 00:23:46.750
Toki ni nagasare kyouri ni hanasareru

00:23:46.850 --> 00:23:49.750
We must continue living our lives

00:23:46.850 --> 00:23:49.750
Kizuna nante kizunajynai

00:23:49.830 --> 00:23:52.360
Without each other.

00:23:49.830 --> 00:23:52.360
Omoumama ikite　

00:23:52.450 --> 00:23:53.320
You should

00:23:52.450 --> 00:23:53.320
Soshite

00:23:53.410 --> 00:23:58.820
Ascend the heavens and look below.

00:23:53.410 --> 00:23:58.820
Nobotta itadakikara mieru

00:23:58.930 --> 00:24:02.610
Show me the scenery in my dreams.

00:23:58.930 --> 00:24:02.610
Keshiki wo oshiete itsuka

00:24:02.670 --> 00:24:08.320
Even though we fall in love and drown in passion,

00:24:02.670 --> 00:24:08.320
Koi ni ochiteku ai ni oboreteku

00:24:08.400 --> 00:24:14.810
I desire my wish fulfilled, above this happiness we both share.

00:24:08.400 --> 00:24:14.810
Watashi no kono shiawase yori kanaetai negai sore wa

00:24:14.870 --> 00:24:20.610
I desire your pursuit of beautiful things.

00:24:14.870 --> 00:24:20.610
Anata no ou utsukushii mono

00:24:22.090 --> 00:24:26.590
So abide by my desire, for eternity.

00:24:22.090 --> 00:24:26.590
Kowasarenaide eien ni

00:24:35.710 --> 00:24:37.470
No way! No way!

00:24:43.130 --> 00:24:45.050
Bigger! Even bigger!

00:24:46.800 --> 00:24:48.650
Kill them all! Every one of them!

00:24:49.380 --> 00:24:52.120
Forgive My Silence.

00:24:53.150 --> 00:24:54.390
To be a warrior or an aesthete?

00:24:55.040 --> 00:24:58.010
That is the question.

00:24:56.560 --> 00:24:59.850
Forgive My Silence
